  "status_text": "One tiny machine gets all forty-eight answers right. Pick a number from 0 to 7 and write it in three binary digits. Now pick a digit and ask if it is 0 or 1. For 5, written 101, the middle digit is 0 and the last is 1. Switch on one wire for the number and one for the question. Lean checked that a circuit of at most 22 AND, OR and NOT gates, each reading at most two wires, answers every time. Can it do the same job with 21? That is the next target (L-meta-25767, L-meta-25762). Proofs are being checked and accepted. Recording and credit resume shortly. Nothing is lost.",
